# ============================================================ 9. COMPONENT DESIGN RULE

Every component must answer:

WHAT IS THIS?

WHY DOES IT EXIST?

WHAT EVIDENCE DOES IT DISPLAY?

WHAT CONTEXT DOES IT REQUIRE?

WHAT RELATIONSHIPS DOES IT EXPOSE?

WHAT ACTIONS ARE SAFE?

Do not create components merely because common UI libraries contain them.

# ============================================================ 10. OX-DX CARD

Do NOT create a generic SaaS card and call it OX-DX.

Define what an OX-DX information surface means.

It should communicate:

object
context
evidence
relation
status

Use:

edges
frames
density
proximity
labels

instead of excessive rounded-card decoration.

# ============================================================ 11. OX-DX PANEL

Panels should feel like inspection surfaces.

Use:

strong hierarchy
clear boundaries
controlled density
technical labels
contextual detail

Avoid:

giant empty containers
excessive shadows
soft floating cards everywhere

